0808744749519974, "top": [[" or", -0.000808744749519974], [" Or", -7.457362174987793]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.3466735780239105, "top": [["\n", -0.3466735780239105], [" check", -1.4638686180114746]]}, {"t": "mod", "lp": -0.7339093089103699, "top": [["mod", -0.7339093089103699], ["cat", -0.7892261743545532]]}, {"t": "probe", "lp": -0.2747093439102173, "top": [["probe", -0.2747093439102173], ["info", -1.4355751276016235]]}, {"t": " xe", "lp": -0.010771561414003372, "top": [[" xe", -0.010771561414003372], [" -", -5.341034889221191]]}, {"t": " c", "lp": -0.001492958515882492, "top": [[" c", -0.001492958515882492], ["\n", -7.151119709014893]]}, {"t": "cs", "lp": -4.1485694964649156e-05, "top": [["cs", -4.1485694964649156e-05], ["cm", -10.55876636505127]]}, {"t": "_mode", "lp": -0.0002593734534457326, "top": [["_mode", -0.0002593734534457326], ["=", -9.567404747009277]]}, {"t": "=", "lp": -0.20903342962265015, "top": [["=", -0.20903342962265015], ["=<", -1.8542512655258179]]}, {"t": "2", "lp": -0.30920252203941345, "top": [["2", -0.30920252203941345], ["...", -2.3574278354644775]]}], "text": "# CCS Modes on Intel Arc (xe driver)\n\nThe `ccs_mode` parameter controls how Compute Slice (CCS) contexts are distributed across the GPU's compute units. This is relevant because the Arc A770 has multiple CCS instances, and how you assign them affects workload scaling.\n\n## The Modes\n\n**ccs_mode 1 (default):**\n- Uses a **single CCS** for all contexts\n- All compute work is serialized onto one compute slice\n- Simplest configuration, best for low-concurrency workloads\n\n**ccs_mode 2:**\n- Distributes contexts across **multiple CCS** instances\n- Enables better parallelism when you have many independent contexts/queues\n- Better for workloads that can leverage multiple compute slices simultaneously\n\n## When to Use Each\n\n**Use mode 1 when:**\n- Running a single workload or low number of concurrent contexts\n- You want predictable, simple behavior\n- Default behavior is usually fine for most single-application use\n\n**Use mode 2 when:**\n- Running **multiple concurrent GPU workloads** (e.g., several inference sessions, multiple compute jobs)\n- You want to maximize throughput across independent contexts\n- Benchmarking or stress-testing to see if multi-CCS scaling helps\n\n## A Note on \"4\"\n\nI'm not certain that **mode 4** is a standard/valid value in the current xe driver. The documented modes are typically **0, 1, and 2**. If you encountered \"4\" referenced somewhere, it may be:\n\n- A newer or experimental value in a specific driver version\n- A typo or misunderstanding of the available options\n- Mode-specific to a particular kernel/driver build\n\nI'd recommend checking your actual driver's supported values with:\n\n```bash\ndmesg | grep xe\n# or\nmodprobe xe ccs_mode=2"}